CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "2c3c43fe-7cff-4324-ad4f-4318aae71ef6",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-22T01:20:48Z",
  "ticket_id": "e1b2-2653",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "Four scripts that currently access .tickets-tracker/ directly are refactored to use ticket CLI subcommands: sprint-next-batch.sh calls ticket next-batch (preserving full flag surface \u2014 flags, output format, and exit codes are identical so callers require no update); sprint-list-epics.sh calls ticket list-epics; purge-non-project-tickets.sh calls ticket purge-bridge; pre-commit-ticket-gate.sh calls ticket exists. All subprocess calls use the ticket dispatcher shim (.claude/scripts/dso ticket <subcommand>), consistent with check-shim-refs.sh enforcement. Each refactored script passes its existing test suite with no behavioral regression. Scripts that become thin wrappers retain their filename for shim compatibility and are added to the boundary hook allowlist with a comment citing this epic.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system state where scripts durably use CLI subcommands instead of direct filesystem access, with ongoing enforcement via shim compatibility"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A check-tickets-boundary.sh pre-commit hook is added to .pre-commit-config.yaml that exits non-zero when any staged non-ticket-system file contains: (a) a direct .tickets-tracker/ reference for ticket data access, or (b) a reference to an absorbed script by its original filename. The hook's closed allowlist contains exactly: ticket-system scripts (plugins/dso/scripts/ticket-*), .suggestions/ accessors (suggestion-record.sh, retro-gather.sh), .review-events/ accessors (emit-review-event.sh, review-stats.sh), exclusion-pattern scripts (capture-review-diff.sh, skip-review-check.sh, compute-diff-hash.sh), thin wrapper scripts from SC1, and legitimate structural documentation (files under plugins/dso/docs/ that describe the directory layout rather than access it \u2014 path-scoped exclusion). Adding to the allowlist requires a comment citing the tracking ticket.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (pre-commit hook enforcement with specific allowlist rules) that persists after implementation, not a one-time task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "All document references in skills, workflows, agent definitions, and CLAUDE.md are updated: references to absorbed scripts use the new ticket <subcommand> syntax; references to direct .tickets-tracker/ access for ticket data are replaced with ticket CLI equivalents. No backward-compatibility shims. The document sweep ships in the same commit batch as the SC1 script refactors to prevent live session regressions in skills that invoke old script names directly. Verified by check-tickets-boundary.sh passing in CI with zero violations.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a completed migration task with verification criteria (check-tickets-boundary.sh passing), not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "test-check-tickets-boundary.sh validates the hook with at minimum: (1) a synthetic violator exits non-zero with an actionable error naming the disallowed reference and the CLI replacement; (2) a staged change to each allowlist member (compute-diff-hash.sh, emit-review-event.sh, suggestion-record.sh, retro-gather.sh, capture-review-diff.sh, skip-review-check.sh) passes with exit 0, confirming the allowlist is not over-broad.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes the durable validation behavior that the test script must continuously perform, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
